# Every file is checked out as committed, LF and all, on Windows too (no
# core.autocrlf conversion): xtask reads committed files byte for byte, and a
# CRLF copy is a different file. A model's chunk list in xtask/models/chunks
# with CRLF is "not a kai-chunks 1 list" (kainet::chunks refuses it), which
# stopped try-it-windows.yml's first boot (run 46110893489); goldens, NOTICES
# and the files baked into the image would differ the same way.
* -text

# decisions.md is append-only: concurrent rows from two branches both stay.
# This only helps our own merges (the batch's merge-tree); GitHub's mergeability check ignores
# it, so a new row is a file in docs/decisions/rows/ instead (see its README). Keep the line until
# the pull requests that still append a row have landed. Never use merge=union on code.
docs/decisions.md merge=union
